# Blocked display names. Copy this file to .env.blocked-names (gitignored) and
# put the real list there; it never goes in the repository.
#
# One term per line: <mode> <term>, terms in lowercase letters and digits.
#
#   contains  blocked anywhere in a name. For terms with no innocent use.
#   word      blocked as the whole name or one underscore-separated part of
#             it. For short terms that hide inside ordinary words.
#   name      blocked only as the whole name, ignoring digits and
#             underscores. For reserved names (staff, the app, the promotion)
#             that are fine inside a longer handle.
#   group     an identity term. Blocked only when the name also has a
#             hostile term somewhere in it.
#   hostile   a word that is only hateful next to an identity term. Blocked
#             only when the name also has a group term.
#   root      blocked anywhere in a name, like `contains`, except inside an
#             `allow` word. For a slur root that also sits inside ordinary
#             words, so spellings built on it are caught. Across an
#             underscore it only counts from the start of a part: with
#             `root zud`, "Kazu_Dean" is fine but "azu_ddy" hides it. A term
#             with no innocent use stays `contains`.
#   allow     an ordinary word with a root inside it. Never blocks; the root
#             inside it doesn't count. Doesn't affect `contains` terms.
#
# Disguises are undone before matching: case, digits as letters, underscores
# and repeated letters. Repeated letters are squeezed, so a term with doubled
# letters gets shorter: keep short terms in `word`.
#
# `contains`, `root` and `word` terms also match with lookalike letters
# swapped in (j, l or y for i, vv for w, ph for f, c or q for k, z for s, v
# for u), as long as the term keeps at least 4 letters once those are folded
# together. A shorter term only matches as written, so list its disguised
# spellings (including sound-alike shortenings) as terms of their own.
#
# Load it with:  node scripts/load-blocked-names.mjs            (local)
#                node scripts/load-blocked-names.mjs --linked   (hosted)

contains badword
word zap
name modbot
group zorp
hostile smash
root zud
allow bazudo
